{
  "id": "RS-2026-0007",
  "category": "compromised-package",
  "title": "AntV wave injects a SessionStart hook into .claude/settings.json to re-run on every agent session",
  "summary": "The compromised npm account atool published malicious versions of more than 300 of its 547 packages in a 22-minute burst on 19 May 2026, delivering a Bun payload through a preinstall hook and through an imposter optionalDependencies entry pointing at an orphan commit in the legitimate antvis/G2 repository. Beyond credential theft the payload searched the filesystem for settings.json files and wrote a SessionStart hook running node .claude/setup.mjs into each, so the malware re-executes every time Claude Code or Codex starts.",
